# Who may publish and subscribe to what. Anything not listed here is refused. No secrets in this file: it names
# users and topics only (passwords are built from the environment at start-up, mosquitto-auth-entrypoint.sh).
# The same rules are in k8s/mosquitto/templates/configmap.yaml; a test compares them.

# The four sensor simulators: each publishes only its own sensor topic.
user sim-pos-01
topic write sensors/pos-transaction

user sim-ticket-timer-01
topic write sensors/service-timing
# It reads the simulated world's staffing level, which the staff-shift sensor publishes.
topic read sim/world/staffing

user sim-staffing-sensor-01
topic write sensors/staff-shift
topic write sim/world/staffing

# The plate-waste node also takes model commands on its own control topic and reports on its own status topic.
user sim-plate-cam-01
topic write sensors/plate-waste
topic read control/edge/plate-waste/sim-plate-cam-01
topic write edge/status/plate-waste/sim-plate-cam-01

# The MQTT-Kafka bridge reads the four sensor topics and nothing else.
user rp-mqtt-kafka-bridge
topic read sensors/pos-transaction
topic read sensors/service-timing
topic read sensors/staff-shift
topic read sensors/plate-waste

# The operator: the only identity that may send a node a command, and it reads the nodes' statuses. A node also
# checks a command's signature with its own key, so this login alone cannot change a model.
user edge-operator
topic write control/edge/plate-waste/+
topic read edge/status/plate-waste/+
